#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.conflictStyle`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:15
msgid ""
"Specify the style in which conflicted hunks are written out to working tree "
"files upon merge.  The default is \"merge\", which shows a +<<<<<<<+ "
"conflict marker, changes made by one side, a `=======` marker, changes made "
"by the other side, and then a +>>>>>>>+ marker.  An alternate style, "
"\"diff3\", adds a +|||||||+ marker and the original text before the "
"`=======` marker.  The \"merge\" style tends to produce smaller conflict "
"regions than diff3, both because of the exclusion of the original text, and "
"because when a subset of lines match on the two sides, they are just pulled "
"out of the conflict region.  Another alternate style, \"zdiff3\", is similar "
"to diff3 but removes matching lines on the two sides from the conflict "
"region when those matching lines appear near either the beginning or end of "
"a conflict region."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.defaultToUpstream`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:25
msgid ""
"If merge is called without any commit argument, merge the upstream branches "
"configured for the current branch by using their last observed values stored "
"in their remote-tracking branches.  The values of the `branch.<current "
"branch>.merge` that name the branches at the remote named by "
"`branch.<current-branch>.remote` are consulted, and then they are mapped via "
"`remote.<remote>.fetch` to their corresponding remote-tracking branches, and "
"the tips of these tracking branches are merged. Defaults to true."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.ff`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:35
msgid ""
"By default, Git does not create an extra merge commit when merging a commit "
"that is a descendant of the current commit. Instead, the tip of the current "
"branch is fast-forwarded. When set to `false`, this variable tells Git to "
"create an extra merge commit in such a case (equivalent to giving the "
"`--no-ff` option from the command line). When set to `only`, only such "
"fast-forward merges are allowed (equivalent to giving the `--ff-only` option "
"from the command line)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.verifySignatures`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:39
msgid ""
"If true, this is equivalent to the `--verify-signatures` command line "
"option. See linkgit:git-merge[1] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.renameLimit`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:49
msgid ""
"The number of files to consider in the exhaustive portion of rename "
"detection during a merge.  If not specified, defaults to the value of "
"`diff.renameLimit`.  If neither `merge.renameLimit` nor `diff.renameLimit` "
"are specified, currently defaults to 7000.  This setting has no effect if "
"rename detection is turned off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.renames`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:54
msgid ""
"Whether Git detects renames.  If set to `false`, rename detection is "
"disabled. If set to `true`, basic rename detection is enabled.  Defaults to "
"the value of diff.renames."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.directoryRenames`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:60
msgid ""
"Whether Git detects directory renames, affecting what happens at merge time "
"to new files added to a directory on one side of history when that directory "
"was renamed on the other side of history. Possible values are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:62
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "`false`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:64
msgid ""
"Directory rename detection is disabled, meaning that such new files will be "
"left behind in the old directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:64
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "`true`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:66
msgid ""
"Directory rename detection is enabled, meaning that such new files will be "
"moved into the new directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "`conflict`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:67
msgid "A conflict will be reported for such paths."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:71
msgid ""
"If `merge.renames` is `false`, `merge.directoryRenames` is ignored and "
"treated as `false`. Defaults to `conflict`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.renormalize`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:82
msgid ""
"Tell Git that canonical representation of files in the repository has "
"changed over time (e.g. earlier commits record text files with _CRLF_ line "
"endings, but recent ones use _LF_ line endings).  In such a repository, for "
"each file where a three-way content merge is needed, Git can convert the "
"data recorded in commits to a canonical form before performing a merge to "
"reduce unnecessary conflicts.  For more information, see section \"Merging "
"branches with differing checkin/checkout attributes\" in "
"linkgit:gitattributes[5]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.stat`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:86
msgid ""
"What, if anything, to print between `ORIG_HEAD` and the merge result at the "
"end of the merge.  Possible values are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:89
msgid "Show nothing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:90
msgid "Show `git diff --diffstat --summary ORIG_HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compact`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:91
msgid "Show `git diff --compact-summary ORIG_HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:96
msgid ""
"but any unrecognised value (e.g., a value added by a future version of Git) "
"is taken as `true` instead of triggering an error.  Defaults to `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.autoStash`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:106
msgid ""
"When set to `true`, automatically create a temporary stash entry before the "
"operation begins, and apply it after the operation ends.  This means that "
"you can run merge on a dirty worktree.  However, use with care: the final "
"stash application after a successful merge might result in non-trivial "
"conflicts.  This option can be overridden by the `--no-autostash` and "
"`--autostash` options of linkgit:git-merge[1].  Defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.tool`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:112
msgid ""
"Controls which merge tool is used by linkgit:git-mergetool[1].  The list "
"below shows the valid built-in values.  Any other value is treated as a "
"custom merge tool and requires that a corresponding `mergetool.<tool>.cmd` "
"variable is defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.guitool`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:118
msgid ""
"Controls which merge tool is used by linkgit:git-mergetool[1] when the "
"`-g`/`--gui` flag is specified. The list below shows the valid built-in "
"values.  Any other value is treated as a custom merge tool and requires that "
"a corresponding `mergetool.<guitool>.cmd` variable is defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.verbosity`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:128
msgid ""
"Controls the amount of output shown by the recursive merge strategy.  Level "
"0 outputs nothing except a final error message if conflicts were "
"detected. Level 1 outputs only conflicts, 2 outputs conflicts and file "
"changes.  Level 5 and above outputs debugging information.  The default is "
"level 2.  Can be overridden by the `GIT_MERGE_VERBOSITY` environment "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.<driver>.name`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:132
msgid ""
"Defines a human-readable name for a custom low-level merge driver.  See "
"linkgit:gitattributes[5] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:133
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.<driver>.driver`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:136
msgid ""
"Defines the command that implements a custom low-level merge driver.  See "
"linkgit:gitattributes[5] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:137
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge.<driver>.recursive`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/merge.adoc:140
msgid ""
"Names a low-level merge driver to be used when performing an internal merge "
"between common ancestors.  See linkgit:gitattributes[5] for details."
msgstr ""
